Unswerving Hammer	21	{"kind":"spell","title":"Unswerving Hammer","wikiPath":"/Unswerving_Hammer","sources":[],"components":[],"rewards":[],"card":{"title":"Unswerving Hammer","icon":"https://eqlwiki.com/images/9/97/Spellicon_L.png","lines":["Summons a magical hammer that attacks your target relentlessly until either the hammer or the target dies. If there are additional mobs on the hammer's hate list, the hammer will stay alive and attack those mobs. The summoning cleric cannot control this hammer at all; e.g., it will always taunt. Using \"Go Away\" is of unknown use. The hammer has approximately 10 hp and cannot receive damage shields. It has a max hit of 40-45 depending on level. It can be given most other buffs once summoned (this was removed in later eras). This spell does work in Plane of Sky and the hammer appears normally there. While the spell lists no range, the hammer will despawn very quickly if the target is not close enough to the hammer to begin an initial attack. The pet may be reclaimed with Reclaim Energy, which increases the utility of the hammer somewhat. This pet is situationally useful for long melee-heavy fights with no AE spells such as Ulump Pujluk or An enraged golem. This spell is called Unswerving Hammer of Faith once scribed.","Classes: Cleric - Level 54","Summon Pet: SumHammer","Mana: 600","Skill: Conjuration","Casting Time: 2.50","Recast Time: 2.25","Fizzle Time: 2.25","Resist: Unresistable","Range","Target Type: Self","Spell Type: Beneficial","Duration: Instant"]},"fetchedAt":"2026-09-05T03:37:42.657Z","outOfEra":false}
